# Vibeboard Product Rule (Global)

## Stack and architecture
- Frontend: React + TypeScript.
- Styling: Tailwind CSS utility-first approach; avoid ad-hoc inline styles.
- Backend and DB: Supabase (Auth, Postgres, Row Level Security, Edge Functions when needed).
- Keep strict type safety across frontend, API layer, and Supabase payloads.

## Core product behavior
- Product is a task board like Trello/Jira with AI features.
- Support global task creation and decomposition: AI splits big goals into actionable subtasks.
- Each subtask must include: owner, status, priority, estimate, deadline, and parent task link.
- Preserve task hierarchy (epic -> task -> subtask) for roadmap and reporting.

## Roadmap requirements
- Roadmap must be generated from task graph and deadlines, not hardcoded static data.
- Respect dependencies between tasks when building timeline views.
- Any roadmap UI change must keep backward compatibility with existing task relations.

## Telegram integration
- Allow task creation via Telegram bot/messages.
- Validate and normalize incoming Telegram payload before creating records in Supabase.
- Store Telegram linkage metadata (chat/user identifiers) separately from business task data.

## Overdue notifications
- Send Telegram notifications when a task deadline is exceeded.
- For management notifications, include per-user summary: overdue count, nearest overdue task, total delay.
- Notifications must be idempotent (no duplicate spam for the same overdue event window).

## Implementation quality
- Prefer small, reusable React components and typed hooks.
- Add/keep tests for AI decomposition logic, overdue summary logic, and Telegram webhook handlers.
- Never weaken Supabase RLS policies to "make it work"; fix access paths correctly.

